---
title: Caramelized Apple Dumplings
author: Mildred McKinzie
category: Desserts
cook time: 1 hour
source: Loving Memories of Mildred
---

@flour{1%cup}
@baking powder{2%tsp}
@salt{1%tsp}
@butter{6%Tbsp}
@milk{6%Tbsp}
@apples (quartered or halved)
@brown sugar{1%cup} (or more)
@butter{4%Tbsp}
@water{1%cup}

Mix flour, baking powder, salt, butter, and milk and roll thin. Cut into squares. Place 1/4 apple or 1/2 small apple in center of each square. Place wrapped apple (seam side down) in pan or baking dish. Add at least 1 cup or more brown sugar over top. Dot with 4 Tbsp butter and add 1 cup water. Bake at 400 degrees for 1 hour. Serve with cream.
